 ! heavy black armor. His legs seem like the massive trunk of the ! oak tree. His broad shoulders 
and helmeted head loom high over ! !your own puny frame, and you realize that his powerful arms coul
d  ! "easily crush the very life from you body. There hangs from his belt  ! "a veritable arsenal of
 deadly weapons: sword, mace, ball and chain,  ! dagger, lance, and trident. He speaks with a comma
nding voice: "  Suddenly a sinister, wrathlike figure appears before you seeming " !to float in the 
air. In a low, sorrowful voice he says, Alas, the  " #very nature of the world has changed and the d
ungeon cannot be found.  " #All must now pass away. Raising his oaken staff in farewell, he fades  "
 "spreading darkness. In his place appears a tastefully lettered sign  " reading: "               
